"Settings.SecretVault.Title" = "Secret Vault";
"Settings.SecretVault.Desc" = "Hide chats behind a PIN of their own, separate from your device passcode. A local lock in this app on this device, not encryption.";
"Settings.SecretVault.Notice" = "Hidden chats disappear from your list in this app and open only after you enter the vault PIN. Long-press a chat and choose \"Add to Vault\" to hide it. Turning this off asks for the PIN and brings all hidden chats back.\n\nThe vault PIN is separate from your device passcode. This is a local lock in this app on this device, not encryption: hidden chats stay in your Telegram account and remain visible in other Telegram clients.\n\nIf you forget the PIN, you can get back in with Face ID or Touch ID (while the enrolled face or fingerprint has not changed) or with the Chat Lock master pincode, if that master was already set when you set the vault PIN (if you create the master later, change the vault PIN once to link them). The device passcode is not accepted.\n\nHidden chats and Chat Lock stay on this device only — they do not transfer to a new device and have to be set up again there.";
"Settings.SecretVault.ChangePin" = "Change Vault PIN";
"Settings.SecretVault.UseSecretCode" = "Reveal with a secret code";
"Settings.SecretVault.UseSecretCode.Desc" = "Open the vault by typing your PIN into chat search instead of holding the \"Chats\" title. Changing this setting asks for the vault PIN.";
"Settings.SecretVault.UseSecretCode.Notice" = "When on, there is no visible gesture: type your full vault PIN into the chat-list search and pause for a moment — the vault opens. If your vault uses a text password, type it and then tap Search.\n\nYour own chats and contacts still appear while you type, but the text stays on this device: nothing is sent to Telegram's search until you tap Search. After several wrong codes, checking pauses for a while.\n\nThe vault PIN is separate from your device passcode and is a local lock in this app on this device, not encryption — hidden chats stay in your Telegram account and remain visible in other Telegram clients. Forgot it? Use Face ID or Touch ID (unchanged enrollment) or the Chat Lock master pincode — the master works only if it was already set when you set the vault PIN; the device passcode is not accepted. Hidden chats and Chat Lock do not transfer to a new device.";
"Settings.SecretVault.RevealHint.Title" = "Secret Vault Enabled";
"Settings.SecretVault.RevealHint.SecretCode" = "Your hidden chats are now safe. To reveal them again later, type your full PIN into the chat search and pause for a moment (with a text password, tap Search after typing it). While this is on, what you type stays on this device — to search all of Telegram, tap Search on the keyboard.";
"Settings.SecretVault.RevealHint.LongTap" = "To open the vault, press and hold the \"Chats\" title at the top of your chat list.";
